WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.969
 

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.574
What does wealth look like to you?

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.576
Is it one hundred dollars?

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.511
A thousand dollars?

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.246
A million dollars?

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.081
We can always go higher.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.021
In today's world, the richest
1% of the population

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:24.190
owns almost half of
the world's wealth.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:30.030
Well, let's level the playing field
and see what we get.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.898
This is 'What If,'

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:35.869
and here's what would happen
if money was distributed equally.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:50.350
That's more money than most countries
produce in goods and services every year!

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.619
After the 2008 financial crisis,

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.687
and the Occupy Wall St. Movement,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:59.459
you're probably aware that wealth
distribution in the world, is, well...

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:05.732
And studies show that the
divide is only getting bigger.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:11.071
But, what if we took all the world's
cash, investments, assets, et cetera,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:15.809
sold them, and gave every person
in the world an equal share?

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.314
We can wage a war on poverty, but,

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.520
If you liquidated all of
the world's productive assets

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.390
and combined them with all
the money in the global economy,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.159
you'd be looking at a huge pile of cash.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.763
Roughly $250 trillion US dollars.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.832
In fact, that's so much money,

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:42.669
that if you stacked that
$250 trillion in 100 dollar bills,

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.572
it would stretch more than
half way to the moon!

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.179
Take $250 trillion

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:57.617
and divide it between the current
world population of 7.7 billion,

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.566
The equal distribution
of the world's wealth

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.769
would certainly give a lot of
people a much needed leg-up.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.240
Those living in extreme poverty
and lower-income households

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.244
could afford more food,
water, clothing, shelter,

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.447
and other necessities that
some of us take for granted.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.587
In a world of 7.7 billion people
who are motivated by different things,

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:38.191
and who have different skillsets,
maybe not long at all.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.394
The first big hurdle
would be financial education.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.830
In order to keep
relative wealth equality,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.965
people would have to
be smart with their money.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.133
Now, that doesn't mean cut out

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.802
all entertainment and
stick to the bare necessities,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:49.836
all entertainment and
stick to the bare necessities, 
but, don't do this...

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.004
but, don't do this...

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.910
We also have to wonder
what would happen

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.947
to the quality of goods and services in
a world where everyone makes the same,

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:04.551
and there's no incentive
to innovate or work harder.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.986
Without strict regulations,
you can imagine how

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:11.791
this egalitarian society could
revert to one very much like our own.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.227
The world is full of entrepreneurs,

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.995
people who are looking to make a buck,

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.632
or simply want to make
a positive contribution to society.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.534
You can see how these people might

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.637
invest their share of
the world's loot into new ideas.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:28.841
They could convince others that the
product of their ideas is worth paying for.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:32.145
And if enough people buy into it,
once again,

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:37.650
the market will give rise to millionaires,
billionaires, and huge corporations.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.487
In short, some people will use
their share to become very rich,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:45.391
while others may fall back into
poverty due to lack of education,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:50.263
or unforseen circumstances
like an illness, or a natural disaster.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.032
But despite a resurgence
of an economic divide,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.235
there's still hope in this scenario.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.905
Universal basic income projects
have been tested around the world

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.940
to generally favorable results.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.508
While some studies revealed that,

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:06.713
when guaranteed a lump sum of money
every year, work effort decreased,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.515
they also showed that
universal basic income

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.284
increased school attendance,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.087
reduced medical costs
in mental health cases,

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:17.190
and was not squandered
on luxury goods.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.093
Universal basic income isn't a new idea,

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:23.263
but we're still learning how
to make it work effectively.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:28.234
Naturally, a perfect world, where everyone
has the same amount of money isn't feasible;

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.402
but that doesn't mean we can't

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:34.307
ensure everyone gets enough
food, water, clothing, and shelter.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:37.610
If you want more than that,
you're gonna have to work for it.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.579
Learn how to be smart with your money,

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:42.415
manage it well, live within your means,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.884
and keep an eye out
for good opportunities.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:48.221
Are you waiting for that billion dollar
idea to pop into your head?

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.656
It won't come on it's own;

00:04:49.656 --> 00:05:00.266
but it might help if you start by
asking yourself, "What If?"

